silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_04_yoneda_for_transport_sections_02_transported_profile_under_full_and_faithful_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'TransportedProfileUnderFullAndFaithfulConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, no clinic arrow is invented: every clinic arrow X' -> F(Mittens) comes from a household arrow; also, no two distinct household arrows collapse to one clinic arrow; also, the clinic hom-set from the patient-image probe to the patient image." .
